  "notes": [
    "Measurement only. No runtime, registry, recipe, catalog, world, selection or migration contract is adopted.",
    "Source family explicitly uses depthCap3 and alignToEndCell:false. Both visual slicing and native collision receive the same sourceModel.",
    "Only edges=0 cells may share; all edges!=0 cells retain recipe identity. Logical facing remains in every key.",
    "Equivalence includes canonical structural cubes with UV/material slots, native collision, and garment cubes with actual texture keys substituted only on emitted faces. Wood materials are identical across all recipes. Unused dye/seam bindings are not counted.",
    "All textile recipes have the same interior linen-only garment output; bare wood has no garment and cannot be equated to linen. Pooling distinct bare and linen profiles in a single block ID still uses separate codebook entries.",
    "A new global assembly recipe would have to be recovered from all relevant loaded perimeter blocks. Pick-block on shared interiors, borderless fragments, partial loading, mixed or damaged perimeters and copying interiors lose current local recipe semantics.",
    "This does not solve those ownership/inference problems. The parent is evaluating whether the measured savings justify a separate contract.",
    "Covered-top overlap at15.91..16 remains unresolved. Counts are from the unchanged structural-plus-garment study, not a rendering approval.",
    "The all-covered-only scenario avoids moving bare cells into a shared pool when doing so adds no sharing benefit.",
    "Dedicated shared-pool IDs add a fixed bank. Hosting generic interior codes in one canonical recipe bank retains perimeter recipe identity and keeps fixed-bank cost at8704, but still changes interior semantics."
  ],
  "inputHashes": {
